==English==
[[File:Ocellate river stingray, Boston Aquarium.jpg|thumb|Ocellate river '''stingray''' (''Potamotrygon motoro'')]]

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|sting|ray}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɪŋˌɹeɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-stingray.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various large, [[venomous]] [[ray]]s, of the [[order]]s {{taxfmt|Rajiformes|order}} and {{taxfmt|Myliobatiformes|order}}, having a [[barbed]], [[whip]]like [[tail]].
#: {{syn|en|stingaree}}
# {{lb|en|US|_|law enforcement}} A [[device]] that [[simulate]]s a [[cell tower]], used to [[intercept]] [[cell phone]] [[communication]]s.
#: {{syn|en|IMSI catcher}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Catherine Nolan; Ashley M. Wilson, JD|title=The Audacity to Spy: How Government, Business, and Hackers Rob Us of Privacy|publisher=Technics Publications|isbn=9781634620604|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=7x3XBgAAQBAJ&lpg=PA74&dq=%22stingray%22%20cell%20tower&pg=PA74#v=onepage&q=%22stingray%22%20cell%20tower&f=false|page=74
|passage=The device mimics a cell phone tower and gets the phone to connect to it. {{...}} Once a signal is found, the '''stingray''' measures its strength and can provide a general location on the map.}}

